National Academies of Sciences, Engineering, and Medicine. 2018. *How People Learn II: Learners, Contexts, and Cultures*. Committee on How People Learn II: The Science and Practice of Learning, chaired by Cora Bagley Marrett. English. [Official front matter](https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/24783/chapter/1); DOI [10.17226/24783](https://doi.org/10.17226/24783).

**Reading:** [chapter 5, Knowledge and Reasoning](https://www.nationalacademies.org/read/24783/chapter/7), followed by chapter 7 for school implications. Compare the account with your own instructional design and distinguish a supported general consideration from an untested local choice.

**Inspection, 1 November 2026:** title/committee/copyright; chapter 5 opening, retrieval and practice sections at pp. 97–101, and explanation/conclusions at pp. 105–106; chapter 7 opening at pp. 135–137. The later chapter 7 assessment section was not retrieved successfully and is not claimed inspected. Whole assigned chapters remain learner reading.

The official HTML was readable. Copyright 2018 National Academy of Sciences, all rights reserved; free access is not an open reuse licence. Link externally; no source media are bundled.
